OL,3,GNEWSA'Let young people lead the way on
OL,4,Aanti-social behaviour'
OL,5,
OL,6,FFor Sienna Ahir and her peers,
OL,7,Fwitnessing the impact of anti-social
OL,8,Fbehaviour has become a normal part of
OL,9,Flife.
OL,11,FThe 17-year-old said it was "very
OL,12,Fcommon" in the West Midlands and it
OL,13,Faffects many young people, whether they
OL,14,Fwere victims, were encouraged to take
OL,15,Fpart or were constantly hyper-alert to
OL,16,Fthe risks.
OL,18,F"You're always exposed to it,
OL,19,Fespecially when you're just walking
OL,20,Fdown the street or taking the bus home
OL,21,Ffrom school," the Wolverhampton teen
OL,22,Fsaid.
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,355,350,200,160,0,100
